<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE electron-iqps9 ascent (3DOF sim)</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Electron &#x27;The Sea God Surveys&#x27; (iQPS Launch 9, QPS-SAR-20) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Method: first-principles 3DOF sim (/workspace/trajectory-deck/sim/ascent3dof.py): WGS-84 rotating Earth, J2, US76 drag,
thrust SL/vac interpolated on ambient pressure, mdot from Isp, staging/fairing/coast events; vertical rise to 8.0 s (rule: config guidance),
pitch kick 3.696 deg over 10 s, gravity turn, linear-tangent upper-stage steering tan(theta)=0.8546-0.002637*(t-t_ign), solved by optimizer.
Vehicle config: Rocket Lab Electron (sim/vehicles/electron.json; every number carries a source URL, derivation, or ASSUMPTION).
Electron: GLOW, S2 propellant, thrusts, Isp, fairing mass/time from Rocket Lab Electron Payload User Guide (7.0 content, 8.0 URL).
DERIVED: S1 propellant (0.90 fraction ASSUMPTION), effective mdot from published burn times; ASSUMED S2 dry 250 kg, Cd 0.4, 8 s vertical rise.
UNTUNED: Rocket Lab has published no mission timeline for this flight; Electron Payload User Guide 8.0 generic event times used.
Inclination not published (iQPS: &#x27;mid-inclined&#x27;); azimuth from NOTAM debris areas.
File ends 2 revs after S2 cutoff on the inferred insertion orbit; Kick Stage (Curie) circularization not modelled (timing unpublished).
Target (see launch config): insertion 230 km, apoapsis 575 km, fpa 0, launch azimuth 107.40 deg; payload 190 kg.
Pad: -39.262833N 177.864469E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s (Earth-relative).
T0 used: 2026-11-02T16:41:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.
POST-CUTOFF: deploy time unpublished (Rocket Lab publishes no deploy or Kick Stage burn time for The Sea God Surveys (mission page: launch time TBD, no timeline as of 2026-10-31); propagated 2 revs on inferred insertion orbit). From insertion T+526.0 s the stage is propagated for TWO revolutions (osculating period 92.94 min) on the inferred insertion orbit (same WGS-84/J2/US76-drag model); rows tagged -coast.
POST-CUTOFF end T+11679 s: inferred insertion orbit, +2 revs (deploy time unpublished): alt 230.0 km, osculating 221.2 x 616.0 km, i 39.955 deg.</description>
